## Prompt contract

Position 1 of `$ARGUMENTS` is a **free-form prompt** (RU/EN) - the scope token, `hard` and any focus text are
optional and may follow in any order. Nobody types keys: resolve scope + depth + focus FROM the prompt.

1. Strip flags. An explicit scope token anywhere wins outright, no scoring.
2. Else score scopes by distinct whole-word keyword hits (table below). Highest unique score wins. Tie -> the
   keyword appearing first in the prompt.
3. Empty arguments -> `session` (default scope), `NORMAL` (default depth), `MEMORY` (default reach); this
   run asks nothing.
4. Outcome-changing ambiguity (e.g. an unresolvable batch split) -> ONE `AskUserQuestion` (max 4 questions)
   BEFORE any work.
5. Prose that is not a scope/reach/id/path is still input: it becomes `{FOCUS}` - emphasis ordering only, never a filter.

Then print this block ONCE, before the first action:

```
PLAN — memory-sync
INPUT:  <arguments verbatim, or "(empty)">
MODE:   <SCOPE> — <explicit | matched keyword: X | default>
SCOPE:  depth=<DEPTH>; reach=<REACH>; focus=<FOCUS interpretation | "standing emphasis">; batches=<batch: N files, ...>
DO:     <2-5 imperative bullets — gather -> sync -> verify -> self-sync -> report>
RESULT: <what the user ends up holding>
```

Labels are literal; values follow the conversation language.

