## Input resolution - THREE ORTHOGONAL AXES

Parse `$ARGUMENTS`. The first token matching a scope keyword sets `{SCOPE}` (default `session`). The token `hard`
anywhere - or the same intent in prose - sets `{DEPTH}` = `HARD`. A reach token anywhere - or the same intent
in prose - sets `{REACH}` = `REFS` (default `MEMORY`). Everything else is free-form `{FOCUS}`.

**`{SCOPE}` selects WHICH CHANGES drive the sync:**

| `{SCOPE}` | Change-fact source | EN keywords | RU keywords | Mutates? |
|-----------|--------------------|-------------|-------------|----------|
| `session` (DEFAULT) | What THIS conversation did: new modules, renames, removals, env vars, migrations, commands, behaviour changes. The COORDINATOR writes the change-fact list from its own context - no gather agent for it | *(empty)*, session, this conversation | сессия, эта беседа | yes |
| `branch` | `git diff $(git merge-base HEAD "$MAIN")..HEAD`, where `$MAIN` is DERIVED (`git symbolic-ref --short refs/remotes/origin/HEAD 2>/dev/null` -> `origin/<name>`, else the bare `{DEFAULT_BRANCH}`; both are valid revisions). NEVER hardcode `main` | branch, diff vs main | ветка, диф с main | yes |
| `commit <sha>` / `commit <a>..<b>` | `git show <sha>` / `git diff <a>..<b>` | commit, sha | коммит | yes |
| `recent[:N]` | `git diff HEAD~N..HEAD`, default N=10 | recent, last N commits | последние | yes |
| `all` | NO diff - EVERY checkable fact in every memory file is re-verified against current code | all, everything, re-verify all | всё, все факты | yes |

**`{DEPTH}` selects HOW HARD:**

| `{DEPTH}` | Behaviour |
|-----------|-----------|
| `NORMAL` (DEFAULT) | fact sync + dedup + compression |
| `HARD` | NORMAL plus the TWO aggressive passes in `references/hard-sync.md`: rules `paths:` PRECISION audit and OBVIOUS-KNOWLEDGE PURGE. Triggered by the token `hard` or semantically ("почисти жёстко", "too much context", "aggressive", "cut it down") |

**`{REACH}` selects WHAT MAY BE EDITED:**

| `{REACH}` | Editable set | Tokens |
|-----------|--------------|--------|
| `MEMORY` (DEFAULT) | the instruction surface below, wherever it lives, tracked or not | *(empty)* |
| `REFS` | MEMORY plus each git-TRACKED reference file that an ALWAYS-LOADED instruction file cites and tells its reader to open, when that file sits OUTSIDE the instruction tree | `refs`, `reach refs`, референсы, со ссылками |

ALWAYS-LOADED means the file reaches context with no gate: a rule with no `paths:` key, the CLAUDE.md family, an
agent or skill body. A rule gated by `paths:` is LAZY - its outside references are REPORTED, never edited, at
either reach.

At `MEMORY` a tracked outside reference is RESOLUTION-CHECKED only: every compression or fact finding on it is
REPORTED, never applied. Blast radius is the reason - such a file has consumers this sweep cannot see (CI, tests,
another tool, a human procedure), while the instruction surface has one consumer class. `REFS` never widens past
the three NON-NEGOTIABLE exclusions: doc-flow paths, source code and secrets stay out at every reach. At `REFS`
each outside file gets its own row in the report, and non-growth still binds.

> **The axes are independent.** `all hard` re-verifies everything AND purges; `session` (no token) is the cheap
> default. Depth never changes which files are swept; scope never changes how hard they are cut; reach changes
> only the editable set, never which files are swept nor how hard they are cut.

**`{FOCUS}` is EMPHASIS ONLY - a hard rule.** Free-form focus text re-ORDERS effort inside the sweep; it NEVER
narrows it, never drops a batch, never skips a file. "only rules" means *rules first and hardest*, not *rules
alone*. A run that touched only one layer because the user named that layer is a DEFECTIVE run.

> **Standing emphasis:** {FOCUS_EMPHASIS}
> Facts stay ahead of dedup, and dedup ahead of compression, whatever the emphasis. The order may be SHARPENED,
> never inverted.

Print the PLAN block from the Prompt contract section above, once, before any work. Fold the fan-out numbers into
its `DO:` bullets:

```
PLAN — memory-sync
INPUT:  {ARGUMENTS verbatim, or "(empty)"}
MODE:   {SCOPE} — {matched token | "default (no scope token)"}
SCOPE:  depth={DEPTH} — {matched signal | "default NORMAL"}; reach={REACH} — {matched token | "default MEMORY"}; focus={FOCUS interpretation | "standing emphasis"} (emphasis only - full surface still swept); batches={batch: N files, ...} (re-enumerated this run)
DO:     gather ({N} Explore) -> sync ({M} agents, one per non-empty batch) -> verify ({K} Explore, one per EDITED batch) -> self-sync -> report
RESULT: memory-sync report + edited files listed in Phase 6
```

