**Git-visibility caveat - derive it EVERY run: compare `git ls-files -- .claude '*CLAUDE.md' '*AGENTS.md'` against
the same surface ON DISK as a SET DIFFERENCE ON PATHS, never a count delta (0 tracked rows = git-ignored; any
on-disk PATH absent from the tracked list = MIXED - the two listings prune differently, so equal totals prove
nothing); it changes when `.gitignore` does.** Visibility here: {GIT_VISIBILITY}. When the surface is git-IGNORED, `git status` / `git diff`
can NEVER account for a memory edit: **never flag a memory file's absence from the diff**. Verification is then by
DIRECT RE-READ of each edited file, and the diff check reduces to PROVING that no source, docs, task-state or
secrets file changed. **MIXED is handled as IGNORED** - the untracked part is invisible to the diff, so re-read
every edited file directly and never flag an absence. Only when the surface is fully git-TRACKED does `git diff`
account for memory edits: assert every edited file appears in it and nothing else does.

Violations -> the coordinator sends targeted fixes back to the responsible batch agent (or fixes a trivial pointer itself), then re-verifies ONLY the fixed files.
**The report may NOT be emitted until every verdict is ok, or the remaining violations are listed as unresolved.**

