## Safety (baked into every phase)

The Phase-2 HARD constraints ARE the safety contract - git read-only, secrets, edit surface, no side effects,
frontmatter, stable ids, non-growth - and they bind the coordinator exactly as they bind a batch agent. Do not
restate them here. One rule lives only at this level:

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Default branch | DERIVE it: `git symbolic-ref --short refs/remotes/origin/HEAD 2>/dev/null` returns `origin/<name>`, the `{DEFAULT_BRANCH}` fallback is a bare name - both are valid revisions. Never hardcode `main` |
